# Code owners for the verification surface.
#
# Purpose: route review requests automatically when someone touches a file that
# decides whether other changes can merge. These paths are load-bearing in a way
# ordinary source is not -- weakening one silently widens what can ship.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT -- do NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" on this repo
# while it is effectively single-maintainer.
#
# GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request. Every PR here,
# including the ones agents open, is authored by @vivekchand, so turning that
# setting on would make every PR permanently unmergeable. CODEOWNERS is used
# here for review ROUTING and visibility only.
#
# The actual anti-tampering enforcement is mechanical instead, and works fine
# with a single maintainer:
#   - tests/test_guard_census.py  -- guard files must exist; the merge gate may
#                                    only grow, never shrink
#   - tests/test_e2e_gate.py      -- the gate must still block what it claims to
#   - tests/test_workflow_yaml_valid.py -- no workflow may silently fail at startup
# Those run in CI and fail the build. They do not need a second human.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner.
*                                   @vivekchand

# The merge gate itself. scripts/e2e_gate.py IS branch protection in practice:
# the single required context "E2E Gate (required)" aggregates whatever this
# file lists, so editing it changes what is allowed to ship.
/scripts/e2e_gate.py                @vivekchand
/.github/workflows/e2e-gate.yml     @vivekchand

# Required-status-check configuration and its watchdog.
/scripts/apply_required_status_checks.py    @vivekchand
/scripts/c6_required_checks_status.py       @vivekchand
/.github/workflows/c6-*.yml                 @vivekchand
/.github/workflows/apply-required-checks.yml @vivekchand

# Bug-class guards. Each of these exists because a specific regression reached
# users; deleting one re-opens that door.
/scripts/check_py39_annotations.py  @vivekchand
/scripts/sync_runtime_count.py      @vivekchand
/scripts/verification_matrix.py     @vivekchand
/scripts/mutation_ratchet.py        @vivekchand

# The declared coverage surface and its recorded baselines.
/verification/                      @vivekchand

# Anti-tampering tests.
/tests/test_guard_census.py         @vivekchand
/tests/test_e2e_gate.py             @vivekchand
/tests/test_workflow_yaml_valid.py  @vivekchand
/tests/test_verification_matrix.py  @vivekchand

# CI definition at large.
/.github/workflows/                 @vivekchand
